-- Scene 4: THE INSTRUMENT CANNOT SEE AN EARCON --
   The audibility floor should bind to Loudness(), the way contrast binds
   to 4.5:1. BS.1770-4 integrates over 400 ms blocks behind a -70 LUFS
   gate, and an earcon is shorter than one block. This is the measurement
   that sent the floor to a substitute metric and SS2 to the plan.
   40 ms at peak 0.50 -> -1000 LUFS
  [ok]   a 40 ms earcon reads as SILENCE (-1000)
   60 ms at peak 0.50 -> -1000 LUFS
  [ok]   a 60 ms earcon reads as SILENCE (-1000)
   100 ms at peak 0.50 -> -1000 LUFS
  [ok]   a 100 ms earcon reads as SILENCE (-1000)
   200 ms at peak 0.50 -> -1000 LUFS
  [ok]   a 200 ms earcon reads as SILENCE (-1000)
   400 ms -- one whole block -- reads -9.38 LUFS
  [ok]   at one full block the very same tone measures
  [ok]   and it is a plausible level for peak 0.5
   the metric in use: K-weighted level over the sound's support (BS.1770 weighting, NOT integrated LUFS)
  [ok]   the metric names itself as not standard LUFS
   a 60 ms tone: integrated -1000, support -10.06
  [ok]   the support measure SEES what integrated LUFS calls silence
   a 400 ms tone: integrated -9.38, support -9.38
  [ok]   and it agrees with the standard where the standard answers
  [ok]   the same tone measures the same at 60 ms and 400 ms

-- Scene 5: the floor is DECLARED, and it can FAIL --
   A sound system that cannot fail an audibility check does not have one.
   The floor is declared rather than measured: measuring a room needs a
   microphone, a consent, and an input this machine may not have.
   declared floor: -40 dB
     Danger: level -13.13 dB, margin 26.87 dB (needs 10)
     Warning: level -13.34 dB, margin 26.66 dB (needs 10)
     Info: level -13.67 dB, margin 26.33 dB (needs 10)
     Success: level -14.31 dB, margin 25.69 dB (needs 10)
  [ok]   every sounding value clears the gate in a quiet room
  [ok]   and an alert is held to a HIGHER bar than a cue
   the same motifs in a -10 dB room: margin -3.13 dB
  [ok]   in a loud room the shipped motifs are REFUSED as inaudible
  [ok]   silence stays lawful in any room

-- Scene 6: PRIORITY -- and why :OverDanger is refused --
   Colour asks what can be READ ON a fill, because text and fill are
   co-present and spatial. Two sounds in one instant do not layer, they
   MASK -- and masking is frequency-selective and asymmetric, so there is
   no fixed answer to what can be heard over danger. The answer is nothing:
   you drop, or you duck.
  [ok]   danger outranks warning
  [ok]   warning outranks info
  [ok]   info outranks success
  [ok]   and muted never contends
  [ok]   a cue under a sounding alert is DROPPED
   reason: pre-empted by a louder meaning still sounding
  [ok]   and so is a warning -- rank, not recency
  [ok]   once the alert is over, a cue passes again
  [ok]   a warning alert does NOT pre-empt danger

-- Scene 7: the same state twice in a tenth of a second is ONE state --
  [ok]   the first report passes
  [ok]   the same value 50 ms later is refused
   reason: refractory: the same value inside 150 ms is one event
  [ok]   a DIFFERENT value is not refractory
  [ok]   and after the window the same value passes
   info drops counted: 2
  [ok]   drops are counted, so 'why did that sound vanish' has an answer
  [ok]   and a value nothing happened to counts zero

-- Scene 8: Rule 18, and the honest answer --
   'Actions must acknowledge the user within 100 ms.' Measured on this
   pipeline: 329 ms of ring plus ~90 ms of device and OS. The compute is
   not the problem -- the burst spends 14-32 us of a 10 ms wake-up. All of
   the budget is QUEUEING.
   trigger to ear: 419 ms
  [ok]   a sound cannot acknowledge inside Rule 18's 100 ms
  [ok]   and the face SAYS so rather than letting a caller assume
  [ok]   it is inside half a second, so this is a budget and not a break

   THE CONSEQUENCE, recorded in plan S.5: on a surface with a screen this
   is not a problem, because the sound was never the acknowledgement --
   the visual state change is, and the sound corroborates. On an eyes-free
   surface Rule 18 is unsatisfiable here, and that is a constitutional
   finding rather than a defect this plane can fix.

